I've been kicking around the idea for a new role:
Astronaut!

Astronauts start with a spacesuit, which confers fire and cold
resistance, and also supplies magical breathing. The accompanying space
helmet makes the wearer impervious to the blinding attacks of ravens.
The downside is that the suit is quite heavy, carries a -1 to dex.
penalty, and it is impossible to become very fast while wearing it.

Astronauts can only be human, but may be of any alignment.  Their
starting stats are all quite good; however, they gain no intrinsics as
they level up.

The astronaut's biggest downfall is that he/she is inept with just
about all weapon types, and will struggle until the quest artifact,
Kirk's phaser (better name welcome!), is found.  The phaser is a
powerful ranged weapon, and when applied, it can stun the enemy it's
pointed at.



